nk":{"fieldSizeRank":5,"finishersRank":2,"finishRateRank":76,"winningTimeRank":8,"winningTimeRankDir":6,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1975,"mensWinner":"Derek PREISS","mensTime":"05:53:00"}},"narrative":"The 2025 Comrades Marathon was the 98th running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban.\n\nTete DIJANA claimed the men's title in 05:25:28, ahead of Piet WIERSMA (05:25:33) and Nikolai VOLKOV (05:29:42). Gerda STEYN won the women's race in 05:51:19, followed by Alexandra MOROZOVA (05:55:56).\n\nGerda STEYN's 05:51:19 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1975 (Derek PREISS, 05:53:00).\n\nFrom a field of 22,702 entries, 18,223 runners crossed the finish line (80.3% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 14,656 men and 3,564 women (19.6% female). The average finish time was 10:18:09.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 31 Wally Hayward, 712 Silver, 6,046 Bill Rowan, 4,820 Bronze, 6,594 Vic Clapham. 4,433 runners (24.3%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Sthembiso MATHONSI in 12:00:00.\n\nThis edition featured the 5th largest field in race history and the 2nd most finishers ever. Compared to the previous down run in 2023, the field was 10.5% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 69% of the finishers, with 5,575 seniors (avg 10:03:57) and 12,526 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}